#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# implies

#% text
# `implies(p, q)` is the logical implication: `true` when `p` is `false` or `q` is `true`, and `q` when `p` is `true`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Otherwise the call stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
implies(false, x)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
implies(true, x)
#% output
#= x

#% cell
implies(p, true)
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
implies(true, false)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
implies(p, q)
#% output
#= implies(p, q)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `and`, `or`, `not`, `xor`
